Z||000000||thecage||10-08-2001||09:49 PM||||i get this code only if i drive the car over 100km hr for a few minutes. the light will stay on until the car is shut off. it will not come back on if doing city driving but once on highway for a few minutes it comes back on. now the egr tube was replaced a week ago with a brand new one so i know it's not that. the egr valve seems to go up and down when i put my fingers up underneath it and push. the only thing i can see out of whack is from the solenoid there is two hoses coming off the one side towards the firewall. one seems connected to something the other one is just hanging off loose going nowhere.<P>once again i'm a recent member and the info here is great.||||reg||1
Z||000001||88CoupeV6||10-09-2001||11:54 AM||||It may be a bad solenoid. I think there was a thread about it a wile ago. <P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/newsig.jpg">    <BR>:D  <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||3
Z||000002||Alex4mula||10-09-2001||12:55 PM||||Check VERY carefully the vacuum hoses for the EGR. I had that problem and when inspected the plastic hoses both had leaks. One was crack and the other had a big 1/4" hole. Replaced them and no more light.||||reg||1
Z||000003||mshill||10-09-2001||01:06 PM||||Also, check your EGR tube (between plenum and EGR valve) if it has a small crack in it it will do this.  replaced mine and it went away.||||reg||1
Z||000004||btoth||10-09-2001||02:20 PM||||If you don't have any vacuum leaks... just replace the EGR valve itself.  $30.  That's probably why the light only comes on when your going fast... mine died, and the light only came on after I drove over 45mph for a while.<P>Can you give a better discription of the loose vacuum line?  I had some pictures of the lines in that area in a thread on vacuum lines in the Tech section from last week. I can repost them if it would help.<p>[This message has been edited by btoth (edited 10-09-2001).]||||reg||2
Z||000005||thecage||10-09-2001||09:12 PM||||After careful inspection the hoses all seem ok and i'm pretty sure the egr valve is ok. How can I test the solenoid.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Old Lar||10-09-2001||09:21 PM||||I get the 32 error code and Check engine light when I push my 87 GT to 80 mph for several minutes.  I've change EGR selinoid, valve, tube, vaccuum lines, and still get it.  It doesn't seem to effect the car's performance or gas economy.  I haven't been able to track the problem down for three years.  I suspect that some where there is a small vaccuum leak that I haven't located.||||reg||1
Z||000007||thecage||10-10-2001||09:37 PM||||Well here is an update to the code 32 problem. After checking all the hoses and lines for any signs of breaks I didn't think that was the problem. I manually pushed on the egr valve and it seemed to be fairly snug but easily moved with little pressure so I thought this was ok. I also ran the car at idle and pushed up on the egr valve and there was a change in idle so I was pretty sure the valve was ok. Next was the solenoid, I took it off the car and removed the small block that is attached to the solenoid with two philips screws. Once apart I found some signs of oxidation and minor corrosion. I cleaned it up real good and sprayed the entire inside of this unit with good quality contact cleaner. I put everything back together making sure the hoses were all clean and no obstructions. I even sprayed the electrical connector with contact cleaner before plugging it in. Lastly disconected the neg. of the battery for 30 seconds. (to clear my 32 code)<P>Took it out for a spin on the highway with my 10 year old son as a witness for about 15 minutes and guess what, NO MORE FRIGGIN' CODE<P>YAH WHOOO!!!<P>I didn't really want to spend $217.00 Cdn for a solenoid. That's what the dealer want's for it. Crazy.||||reg||1
Z||000008||88CoupeV6||10-11-2001||03:29 PM||||Great,  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Glad to hear that.||||reg||7
